  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm {Lyman}$<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/wSAeXyCMu9BKFFvtVIVjtMNL93auGqE9vlsjs9KJe3A.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_1}=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right]=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{R}}{4}$<br/>$\\lambda_1=\\frac{4}{3 R}$ ________...(1)<br/>and $\\mathrm {Balmer}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/w29yF_Vg6jQYROp0sp8hywsZsevYvY96vx0L_1SX_xo.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\frac{1}{\\lambda_2}=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{9}\\right]=\\frac{5 \\mathrm{R}}{36}$<br/>$\\lambda_2=\\frac{36}{5 R}$<br/>Then, $\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2}=\\frac{5}{27}$",
    "image": null
